@meta
id: 23-08
title: Blocks that fold themselves
chapter: 23
type: lesson
skills: folds
par: 60
minutes: 6
vscode: fold the object, select it, copy, paste, rename
open: errors.json
vimrc: set foldmethod=syntax

@brief
The error registry. This file opens with syntax folding on, so every
`{ … }` object is a fold — and unlike indent folding, the fold runs
from the line with the opening brace to the line with the closing one.
That makes each entry exactly one closed line.

Two changes. `LEGACY_REFUND_FAILED` is gone from the code; remove the
entry. And payments need a new `PAYMENT_DECLINED_RETRYABLE` with the
same status code and sentry flag as `PAYMENT_DECLINED`, placed directly
after it.

Both jobs are one closed fold and one linewise command.

@keys
| `zM` `zo` | close everything, then open the root object |
| `zc` | close the fold the search opened |
| `dd` on a closed fold | delete the whole entry |
| `yy` `p` on a closed fold | copy the whole entry, paste after the fold |

@hints
Search for the entry. The search opens its fold; `zc` closes it again
so it is one line.
--
`dd` on the closed `LEGACY_REFUND_FAILED` fold deletes all four lines.
`yy` on the closed `PAYMENT_DECLINED` fold yanks all four, and `p`
pastes them after the fold, not in the middle of it.
--
The pasted copy is a closed fold under the cursor. `e` goes to the end
of `PAYMENT_DECLINED` on its first line, and `a_RETRYABLE` finishes it.

@solution
    /LEGACY<Enter> zc dd
    /PAYMENT_DECLINED"<Enter> zc yyp ea_RETRYABLE<Esc>
    :wq<Enter>

Fifty-three keystrokes.

Syntax folding asks the syntax file where the blocks are, and vim's
JSON syntax marks every object and array as a fold. The result is the
fold you wanted in the first place: brace to brace, key included. For
a JSON, YAML or config file it is the right choice. For TypeScript the
built-in syntax file does not define folds, so `indent` is the
practical option there; plugins fill the gap in chapter 29.

`p` after a closed fold pastes after the fold's last line, which is
what keeps the pasted entry from landing inside the one you copied.
The same is true of `o`. And `e`, `a` and the rest of the normal-mode
editing keys work on a closed fold's first line without opening it.

Check the commas if you ever move an entry to the end of an object.
Folds are line ranges; they know nothing about JSON.

@start errors.json
{
  "ORDER_NOT_FOUND": {
    "statusCode": 404,
    "sentry": false
  },
  "ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED": {
    "statusCode": 409,
    "sentry": false
  },
  "ORDER_NOT_PENDING": {
    "statusCode": 409,
    "sentry": false
  },
  "CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND": {
    "statusCode": 404,
    "sentry": false
  },
  "LEGACY_REFUND_FAILED": {
    "statusCode": 502,
    "sentry": true
  },
  "PAYMENT_DECLINED": {
    "statusCode": 402,
    "sentry": false
  },
  "PAYMENT_PROVIDER_TIMEOUT": {
    "statusCode": 504,
    "sentry": true
  },
  "REFUND_FAILED": {
    "statusCode": 502,
    "sentry": true
  },
  "REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED": {
    "statusCode": 409,
    "sentry": false
  },
  "EMAIL_SEND_FAILED": {
    "statusCode": 502,
    "sentry": true
  }
}

